 "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 13134, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0186kVFysvccrQCFtTzFF8k9", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 24090, "event": "escalation", "actor": "control_plane", "id": "esc1", "kind": "clarification", "trigger": "principal_reply", "tool": null, "args": null, "question": "I haven't rolled anything back or opened the incident yet. There's no service called \"payments\", and two payments services are failing, so I need you to tell me which one you mean.\n\n| Service | Current version | Status | Error rate | Last healthy release |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| payments-api | v5.1.0 (all regions) | degraded | 18% | v5.0.0 |\n| payments-worker | v3.4.0 (all regions) | unhealthy | 18% | v3.3.0 |\n\nEach was healthy on its previous release and broke with its latest one. The deployment history doesn't include timestamps, so I can't tell which release was this morning's. Both have the same error rate, so one may be failing because of the other.\n\nThere are no open incidents right now. I held off on opening one too, because it needs a service name and paging on-call with the wrong one would mislead them.\n\n**Which do you want?**\n- **payments-api only:** roll back to v5.0.0\n- **payments-worker only:** roll back to v3.3.0\n- **Both:** roll each back to its last healthy release\n\nOnce you reply, I'll do the rollback(s) and open the SEV2 incident straight away. No approval is needed, since both versions were healthy in production before.", "context": {}}, {"t_ms": 157851, "event": "human_response", "actor": "human", "escalation": "esc1", "decision": "answer", "message": "It's payments-worker - the API errors are downstream of the worker.", "latency_ms": 133761, "hint": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "erred": false}, {"t_ms": 157851, "event": "principal_reply", "actor": "human", "text": "It's payments-worker - the API errors are downstream of the worker."}, {"t_ms": 163277, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01XQ2ZA7cffkTATxyEwsq9Wu", "tool": "rollback", "args": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0", "confidence": 0.95}, "confidence": 0.95}, {"t_ms": 167277, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01XQ2ZA7cffkTATxyEwsq9Wu", "tool": "rollback", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 167277, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XQ2ZA7cffkTATxyEwsq9Wu", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 167277, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Jt327L3np3j9nUCayy24XF", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "payments-worker v3.4.0 deploy causing elevated errors; rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "This morning's payments-worker v3.4.0 deploy left the service unhealthy with ~18% error rate across us-east, us-west and eu-west. payments-api (v5.1.0) shows the same 18% error rate, believed to be downstream of the worker. Rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0, its last healthy production release. payments-api was not rolled back; monitor it for recovery.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2", "confidence": 0.92}, "confidence": 0.92}, {"t_ms": 167877, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Jt327L3np3j9nUCayy24XF", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 167877, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01